remarks.para:
The JSON schema emitted for each event is a compact, flat JSON line intended for hot-path processing. Each line represents a single trade or quote object:
{"timestamp":"…","symbol":"SPY","price":100.01,"size":200,"aggressor":1,"sequence":42}
Quote events follow a similar shape with bid/ask-specific fields. This schema is specific to the hot-path pipeline and does not include the higher-level MarketEvent envelope (such as type or payload).

member.summary:
            Deterministic conflict-authority policy. Selects the default winner from the precedence ladder:


golden-copy source (the configured authority) wins outright;

otherwise the higher-ranked source in SourcePrecedence wins;

otherwise (equal rank) the fresher source (by FreshnessAsOf) wins;

otherwise the higher confidence score wins.

            Bulk eligibility is derived from the structured Recommendation: equivalent dismissals stay
            eligible regardless of winner, while accept-winner/accept-challenger recommendations stay eligible
            only when the policy winner matches the recommended source (otherwise they fall back to per-row review).
